@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

#
# prima-materia - two searches carried in the rabbinic law of sorcery
#
# The first is the search that examinations/searches-harba-de-moshe.ttl named on
# 2026-09-24 and did not carry, calling it the first thing the next run at that
# corpus should do. It is carried here and it found places; the nodes it yielded
# stand in traditions/rabbinic-halakhah.ttl.
#
# The second was put to the same part of the same corpus and came back empty,
# and that emptiness is the point of entering it: this transmission applies
# criteria to a performance somebody saw, and it states no condition under which
# a prescribed procedure would have failed. Both searches are therefore about
# the same asymmetry from opposite sides.
#

pmp:RabbinicCounterTransmissionSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the transmission that forbids the art names a criterion for a claimed performance"@en, "Ob die Ueberlieferung, die die Kunst verbietet, ein Kriterium fuer eine behauptete Verrichtung nennt"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Mishnah Sanhedrin VII.11 and Tosefta Sanhedrin XI.5c, trans. Herbert Danby, Tractate Sanhedrin: Mishnah and Tosefta (London: Society for Promoting Christian Knowledge, 1919), pp. 106-107; and Babylonian Talmud, Synhedrin folios 67a to 68a, trans. Lazarus Goldschmidt, Der babylonische Talmud, vol. VII (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1903), pp. 285-290" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the rabbinic legal transmission, which prohibits the operations an operative handbook of the same language and region prescribes, states any criterion by which a performance claimed to have worked is judged: a distinction between a deed and an appearance, a residue a real deed would leave, a test anybody could apply. The question was put because the handbook in traditions/hekhalot.ttl carries a hundred and thirty-six operations and, by the search at pmp:HarbaDeMosheDefectusSearch, no condition of failure anywhere among them, and because the counter-transmission to that silence had been named and not read." ;
    pm:searchTerms "Danby's volume was read at the subject heading for the sorcerer and the two paragraphs under it, found by searching the full text for Sorcerer, and the pages before and after were read for the context and the page sequence. Goldschmidt's seventh volume was located by the Hebrew of the Mishnah, the strings for the one who holds the eyes, for the sorcerer, for the cucumbers and for the holding of the eyes in the Aramaic, and then read continuously in German from the running head 285 to the running head 291, with the Hebrew column stripped so that the two did not run together. The permission to learn was located by the Hebrew for thou shalt not learn, for to understand and for to teach. The German column was also searched for the household above, for the drum, for the camel and for the eye-deception. Rodkinson's English of 1902 was fetched for comparison and measured against Goldschmidt at three places." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:SanhedrinSorcererIsTheOneWhoDoesTheDeed, pmc:SanhedrinBloodAndDungAsTheTraceOfTheDeed, pmc:SanhedrinWaterDissolvesTheTransformation, pmc:SanhedrinThreefoldDivisionOfTheLaw, pmc:SanhedrinWhatIsBeyondTheDemons, pmc:SanhedrinSorceryContradictsTheHeavenlyRetinue, pmc:SanhedrinNothingBesideHimEvenInSorcery, pmc:SanhedrinWhetherTheArtPrevailsAgainstTheDecree, pmc:SanhedrinLearningIsPermittedToUnderstandAndToTeach, pmc:SanhedrinTheSorcererIsStoned, pmc:SanhedrinThreeHundredRulesOnTheWitch ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-01" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-01" ;
    skos:note "The find is a criterion of a kind the holding did not carry. At pmc:SanhedrinBloodAndDungAsTheTraceOfTheDeed a performance is judged by the residue a real deed would have left, by a man who did not see it, from a report by a man who did. Every other criterion in this holding is a sign announced to a practitioner beforehand, which he afterwards reports. This one is negative, cheap, and cannot be supplied by expectation."@en ;
    skos:note "The second find is that the transmission does not keep one criterion. The same discussion also carries the water that dissolves an enchantment at a market in Alexandria, on the opposite premise: there the test ends a transformation the text treats as having occurred. The two are not harmonised in the text, and a reader who meets only one of them will misreport the transmission."@en ;
    skos:note "What the search does not establish. Neither of these texts names the handbook and the handbook names neither of them; the juxtaposition is the compiler's, and no node of this run claims otherwise. What is established and dated is that the Mishnah was fixed around the year two hundred and the Babylonian discussion is carried by names of the third and fourth centuries, while every dating of the handbook now defended in the field puts it later; only the editor's own early dating of 1896 would reverse that. The handbook's silence about failure is therefore a silence against a known norm and not a state of innocence. The datings themselves are modern scholarship and enter this holding only as evidence at an examination, never as a source here; they are named in the issues of this run."@en ;
    skos:note "A finding about the editions, which cost the run a comparison and should save the next one the same. The public-domain English of 1902 is defective for this subject in three measured places: at the permission to learn in tractate Sabbath it omits the whole proof, which its own explanatory remarks announce as method, since where the original gives two statements separated by a formula of alternative it translates only the second; at the name of the art it loses the acrostic and renders the ground of the name as an aside; and the dispute it attaches names the wrong authority to the wrong word. Goldschmidt's German is complete at all three, prints the Aramaic beside it, and carries an apparatus with a printed key to its sigla. For this corpus the German is the edition and the English is not."@en ;
    skos:note "An open question the search raised and did not settle. Goldschmidt's apparatus carries a note at the word of liability in the first clause of the Mishnah, giving it for the Munich manuscript, while his base text, the censorship-free Bomberg edition of Venice 1520 to 1523, is rendered without it, and Danby's English likewise reads the clause as a definition. With the key alone the direction of the variant cannot be settled, and whether the first clause of this Mishnah is a definition or a penal norm turns on it. The place where it is decidable is Strack's edition of the tractate of 1910, which prints the Mishnah from manuscripts and old prints and was not found on the regular route in this run."@en .

pmp:RabbinicDefectusSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the part read states any condition under which a procedure would have failed"@en, "Ob der gelesene Teil irgendeine Bedingung nennt, unter der eine Verrichtung misslungen waere"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Babylonian Talmud, Synhedrin folios 67a to 68b, trans. Lazarus Goldschmidt, Der babylonische Talmud, vol. VII (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1903), pp. 285-291" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Any sentence in the part read saying what would show that one of the operations this transmission reports had not worked, what to do if it did not, a term after which nothing more comes, a repetition on failure, or a defect in the operator or the material that would prevent the effect. The two criteria the discussion does carry judge a performance somebody has already seen; the question here is whether anything judges a procedure beforehand." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The German column of the part read, with the Hebrew and Aramaic stripped out so that the two did not run together, searched for: misslingt, misslang, Misslingen, wirkt nicht, vergeblich, umsonst, gelingt nicht, nicht gelingen, gelingt, wiederhol, Frist, unwirksam, nichts geschieht, vermag nicht, Probe, all of them with no hit at all; Zeichen, one hit, and it is a sign of puberty in the following chapter; pruefen, one hit, and it is the water at the market; kannst, one hit, and it is R. Hanina telling the woman to try. The part was then read through again to see whether such a condition stood anywhere without those words." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-01" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-01" ;
    skos:note "Nothing, and the shape of the nothing is informative. This transmission is unusually well supplied with tests and unusually empty of conditions of failure, and the two are not in tension: its tests are forensic. They are put to a performance that has been exhibited, by somebody deciding whether a deed was done, and that is a different instrument from a condition told to a practitioner in advance. Of the two performances it reports of its own teachers, the calf and the field of cucumbers, neither carries a condition of any kind."@en ;
    skos:note "The limit of the finding, and it is a real one. The search covers seven printed pages of one tractate and no more. The place in this transmission where a numbered condition is known to stand is the rule of the proven amulet in tractate Sabbath, where a thing counts as proven when it has healed and repeated and done so a third time; that place was not opened in this run and no node rests on it. It is named in the issues as the next and cheapest continuation, and in the public-domain English it is reachable as well as in the German."@en .
